"# Function growth\n\nPreview function moves with aos-grow; real runs rewrite config and can move or delete files.\n\n```sh\naos-grow --dry-run up --to dir --name think --take brain.py fsm.json#/states/think/exec\naos-grow up --to file --name idle fsm.json#/states/idle/exec    # writes idle.json; the slot becomes \"idle\"\naos-grow --dry-run down fsm.json#/states/idle/exec             # back to inline; would remove idle.json\n```\n\nCALLER names the config slot that says what to run. up moves an inline instruction to NAME.json (`--to file`) or NAME/_entry (`--to dir`) and changes the slot to \"NAME\"; `--to` is required. down shrinks a folder containing only _entry to a file, or a file to inline; the slot must be exactly a name. Shared targets cannot shrink to inline. Relative references are rewritten to point to the same places.\n\n`--dry-run` goes before up/down and writes nothing. `--take` repeats, is only for `--to dir`, and must name a path in the instruction. `TargetBad` or `NameBad` needs a corrected target/name, not a blind retry. Code that reads AOS_CF/AOS_CD/AOS_CO itself may observe changed locations.\n"
